                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "63820e90-fc0a-30ce-8853-def92df8cf7e",
                        "entry_id": "5d2ca60a-d7ca-3565-bdd9-a7cf91cc8a45",
                        "glosses": [
                            "нар.-поэт., мифол. воплощение смерти [I.1], аллегорическая фигура, изображающаяся обычно в виде скелета в длинном чёрном плаще (или белом саване) c косой и склянками; смертный призрак"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1276712e-43c7-4421-952f-44ff7dda4109",
                                "sense_id": "63820e90-fc0a-30ce-8853-def92df8cf7e",
                                "text": "Будете вот сидеть на своём чемодане, а в один погожий денёк явится к вам костлявая ― и косой по шее."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "792d3bf2-76d6-4c8e-91dd-2c5c01ea1433",
                                "sense_id": "63820e90-fc0a-30ce-8853-def92df8cf7e",
                                "text": "— Я доктор, знаю, что смерть неотвратима. Нет, я не кокетничаю, дескать, приходи ко мне, костлявая, мне без разницы."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4576be5b-1a81-4246-956e-ffd7d9ea25a4",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d2ca60a-d7ca-3565-bdd9-a7cf91cc8a45",
                        "source_sense_id": "63820e90-fc0a-30ce-8853-def92df8cf7e",
                        "target_lang_word": "Death",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Death",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19868378-acbb-3f97-9fc3-11b61d1daf8d",
                                        "entry_id": "ff0699bd-39e3-339d-b4d1-288bee32abd2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The personification of death, often a skeleton with a scythe, and one of the four horsemen of the apocalypse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e03fa55-8f64-4f60-bb94-58a93fb692de",
                                                "sense_id": "19868378-acbb-3f97-9fc3-11b61d1daf8d",
                                                "text": "Death can be seen on a tarot card."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6390e876-ce76-4e16-8a3d-19e57d2b1d9d",
                                                "sense_id": "19868378-acbb-3f97-9fc3-11b61d1daf8d",
                                                "text": "7 And when hee had opened the fourth seale, I heard the voice of the fourth beast say, Come and see.\n8 And I looked, and behold, a pale horse, & his name that sate on him was Death, and hell followed with him: and power was giuen vnto them, ouer the fourth part of the earth to kill with sword, & with hunger, and with death, and with the beastes of the earth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1cc5816-dc8d-46b0-95d7-b3155b0316a1",
                                                "sense_id": "19868378-acbb-3f97-9fc3-11b61d1daf8d",
                                                "text": "Oh cold, cold, rigid, dreadful Death, set up thine altar here, and dress it with such terrors as thou hast at thy command: for this is thy dominion!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4faa311a-00bd-4bf9-a7e9-e8861b5210ea",
                                                "sense_id": "19868378-acbb-3f97-9fc3-11b61d1daf8d",
                                                "text": "He had drunk more than was fit for him, and he was singing some light song, when he saw approaching, as he said, the pale horse mentioned in the Revelation, with Death seated as the rider."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8c0f74d6-1b0c-4aa3-ae69-4a39629cfb2e",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d2ca60a-d7ca-3565-bdd9-a7cf91cc8a45",
                        "source_sense_id": "63820e90-fc0a-30ce-8853-def92df8cf7e",
                        "target_lang_word": "Grim Reaper",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Grim Reaper",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                        "entry_id": "6159d01c-03e0-3cc7-a52f-13309e52d8b8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A personification of Death as an old man, or a skeleton, carrying a scythe, taking souls to the afterlife."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5a163d2-0fde-4ef2-832d-417db8e7b901",
                                                "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                                "text": "Her husband was dead, and Werper fancied that he could replace in the girl’s heart the position which had been vacated by the act of the grim reaper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74c84c06-1bed-42ae-b2eb-3c3566084769",
                                                "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                                "text": "\"Golly, I feel like the devil!\" muttered Anthony dispassionately. Relaxing, he tumbled back upon his pillow. \"Bring on your grim reaper!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e106e0b6-12b2-4896-923c-c4d486cff21e",
                                                "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                                "text": "Mary, will you be mine? Shall we go round together? Will you fix up a match with me on the links of life which shall end only when the Grim Reaper lays us both a stymie?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70458acd-3937-4333-b6a4-10bc884d563f",
                                                "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                                "text": "On the one hand, we had a scenario where, effectively, the American admiral just went \"You know what, all the destroyers attack\", at which point they mowed through the Japanese destroyers like a Grim Reaper through a harvest of very, very dead gorn, especially with the Brooklyns in support."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8c04afa-db50-4ec6-a96d-d2c15dd207ca",
                                                "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                                "text": "But that is the likely outcome if the railway waits for Treasury's grim reaper to come a-calling."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": [
